nor Society etc my  friends were what today we call the  smart alternative students yet for seven  several months prior to the hospital  admission I had been shrinking my  handwriting got smaller and smaller  gradually the differentiation between  lowercase and capital letters  disappeared my English teacher told me  he'd no longer read my papers if I  continued to write like that my voice  volume diminished until I was almost  inaudible I stopped speaking in the  first person I couldn't say the word  in the hospital I admitted I wanted to  die but I was unable to articulate my  reasons for this beyond saying that I  was crummy and bad my thinking and  ability to express myself had shrunk  along with my voice and my handwriting  all I wanted to do was disappear the  hospital psychological testing report  referred to my slipping into a quicksand  like illness deeply depressed with  suicidal preoccupations and fantasies  along with suicidal ideation my symptoms  included insomnia depersonalization and  derealization we would say now that I  was varied  I was described as shy fearful  obsequious dependent and infantile  emotionally while my inability to  express myself was identified as  stubborn stubborn resistance and  withholding my inaccessibility annoyed  and frustrated the psychiatrist treating  me less than two weeks after being  admitted I was started on a course of 25  EC T's I began to experience  hallucinations my nightmares increased  during the day I remained passive and  withdrawn if I had arrived 20 years  later in 1980 let's say I would probably  have been diagnosed with borderline  personality disorder  another critical diagnosis associated  with permanent disability which had  achieved prominence by then 20 years  after that in 2000 perhaps these same  symptoms might have led to a diagnosis  of bipolar disorder although some few  might have suspected PTSD I might be I  might be given any of these diagnoses if  my young self turned up today depending  