hot treatment itself was traumatic  I understood that ECT it induced a  seizure by sending electrical impulses  into the brain I've  figured that all it took was a slight  miscalculation to end up electrocuted as  a consequence I approached every single  treatment terrified I was sure I was  about to be killed  I showed no initial improvement with the  ECT and I developed some symptoms in the  hospital that had not been evident prior  to my admission such as hallucinations  and stuttering serious clumsiness and  eventually seizures I looked like I was  12 although I was 17 when I was admitted  I was smart but I talked pretty dumb  expressing myself more like a  six-year-old than a high achieving  youngster of 17 or 20 I was determined  to die not to escape my own pain but to  atone for my sins no one stepped back to  look at these as valuable clues as  messages that I could not communicate  with words yet was refusing to  relinquish I was acting out in metaphor  what I could not know or say directly  similarly on the level of metaphor the  hospital doctors delivering shock  treatment were unwittingly repeating the  abusive behavior I was fleeing  reinforcing the message that I deserve  to be punished and should never speak  about or even recognize what I knew  after several dismal months I was  assigned to a new young psychiatrist who  was lively and liked me slowly I began  to get better I had been admitted in May  and I returned to school complete my  junior year the following April  commuting from the hospital I returned  to live at home on an extended visit a  six-month pass and in June just a year  after my admission that fall I was  elected president of my high school  National Honor Society  I had a leading role in the school play  I was an illustrator for the yearbook  I took honors classes then less than two  months into my senior year senior year I  began to have seizures and dissociative  episodes  school I began to slip after about seven  months at home 